 result←object(State ∆Pen)arg;style;color;size;pen;next;thispen
 ⍝ Create and return a Pen "handle", which itself contains the properties used for creating pen-based objects
 ⍝ This handle should be "freed" later with '#' ∆WI '⎕Free'

 ⍝ '?Pen' style [fgcolor] [size]

 thispen←(_pen:⍬ ⋄ _color_:State._color_) ⍝ A place to hold the parsed input
 {}object(thispen Pen)arg ⍝ Call the standard pen-parsing routine to fill in the normalized parameters

 :If ¯1=⊃thispen._pen ⍝ If they just gave us an old handle
     result←2⊃thispen._pen ⍝ Just return it as-is and do nothing
 :Else
     ⍝ Build a "handle" namespace out of this definition for later reference; all it needs is the final property-list
     result←'Pen'CreateHandle(Props:DefinePen thispen) ⍝ Turn it into a property-list for creation and store that creation vector
 :EndIf
